0200: CPU clocks follow the load (bluecpu_dvfs, on by default)

0106/0139 left Silver at 1766 MHz and Gold at 2649 MHz all boot. A kernel
thread now ticks every 20 ms: each core's idle time comes from recount
(blue_cpu_idle_abs in osfmk/kern/recount.c), each cluster takes its busiest
core and asks OSM for the lowest level at or above current kHz * busy / 80%.
At 90% busy it jumps to a "hispeed" level (1228 / 1459 MHz) and from there
to the top; it goes up at once and down only after 60 ms of lower wants.
SweetHID's touch and key events (blue_cpu_input) hold at least 1228 / 1459
MHz for 1 s. The 0143 guard caps Gold through the governor when both are on.
A line every 10 s per cluster: average busy, changes, time per level.
bluecpu_dvfs=0 keeps the fixed top levels.

